<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Climbing Logbook</title>
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="./-/favicon-32.png">
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href="./-/favicon-16.png">
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#ff2727">
  {# #470 -- starts the brand font fetch during initial HTML parsing
       instead of waiting for layout to discover it via climbing-header.js's
       own @font-face rule, shrinking the FOUT window (font-display: swap
       still applies -- this doesn't eliminate the swap, just gets the
       fetch started sooner). Always the absolute /-/... path,
       matching climbing-header.js's own hardcoded @font-face url()
       exactly, regardless of this page's own relative-path convention for
       other assets below -- the preload only helps if its URL matches the
       eventual font request byte-for-byte. #}
  <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" href="/-/fonts/BebasNeue-Regular.woff2" crossorigin>
  {# Same shared stylesheet/font/favicon assets as public/-/ and
       the other apex pages (public/register/, public/login/) -- see
       public/login/index.html's own comment for why these are referenced
       rather than duplicated. #}
  {# #857 -- the ?v= query (see .eleventy.js's own comment; #961: a per-file content hash in production builds, and deliberately not printed here, since that would make every build's HTML differ)
       lets public/_headers cache these two files immutably; skipped in
       dev (isDevBuild), which doesn't need it (see app-layout.njk's own
       fuller comment on why). #}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="./-/tailwind.css{% if not isDevBuild %}?v={{ assetVersion }}{% endif %}">
  {# Shared design tokens + <climbing-header> Custom Element (#345).
       Classic script, not a module -- must run synchronously here, before
       first paint. See the file's own comment for why. #}
  {# #1015 -- the brand lockup SVG the header <use>s: fetched during parsing,
       content-hashed by the build, and pre-cached by the service worker. #}
  <link rel="preload" as="image" type="image/svg+xml" href="/-/brand-lockup.svg{% if not isDevBuild %}?v={{ assetVersion }}{% endif %}">
  <script src="./-/components/climbing-header.js{% if not isDevBuild %}?v={{ assetVersion }}{% endif %}"></script>
  <script>
    (function () {
      var stored = localStorage.getItem("logbook_theme");
      var theme = stored || (matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: light)").matches ? "light" : "dark");
      document.documentElement.dataset.theme = theme;
    })();
  </script>
</head>
<body class="bg-background text-foreground font-sans min-h-screen flex items-center justify-center px-4">
  {# #352 -- hidden until session-redirect.js's get-session check
       resolves: a logged-in visitor never sees this marketing content at
       all (redirected straight to their own /log), a logged-out one gets
       it revealed. display:none (not the [hidden] attribute) so this
       works without depending on styles/tailwind.css's own [hidden]
       override (public/-/index.html's own comment on that same
       subtlety) having loaded yet. #}
  <div class="w-full max-w-[440px] text-center" id="page-content" style="display:none">
    <climbing-header variant="brand"></climbing-header>
    <p class="text-muted mb-8">
      Track your boulder and lead sends and projects, by grade and by
      place. Works offline, installable as a PWA. Share a read-only view
      of your log with a public profile page if you want to.
    </p>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 mb-8">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="./register/">Sign up</a>
      <a class="btn" href="./login/">Log in</a>
    </div>

    {# #251 -- a real visitor's other way in before committing to an
         invite code: three pre-seeded, read-only accounts, no signup
         needed. A disclosure popover (not a full modal, client/modal-
         utils.js's createDisclosure() pattern hand-rolled in
         demo-picker.js since this page has no bundled client/ module
         graph to import it from), matching this issue's own "opens a
         popup" wording. #}
    <div class="relative mb-8" id="demo-picker-wrap">
      <button type="button" class="btn w-full" id="demo-picker-trigger" aria-haspopup="listbox" aria-expanded="false">View a demo first</button>
      <div class="absolute top-[calc(100%+.4rem)] left-0 z-20 bg-background border border-border rounded-app p-[.35rem] w-full shadow-[0_8px_24px_color-mix(in_srgb,black_35%,transparent)]" id="demo-picker-popover" role="listbox" aria-label="Choose a demo persona" hidden>
        <div id="demo-picker-list"></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {# #876/#878 -- a real visitor's third way to learn more before
         signing up or trying a demo, alongside those two -- /help is
         reachable logged-out same as this page. #}
    <p class="text-sm text-muted mb-8">Browse the <a class="text-accent" href="/help/">help section</a> to learn more.</p>

    {# Closed beta (#296) -- registration needs a real invite code right
         now; this is a static page with no way to read BETA_GATE_ENABLED
         server-side, so the note stays regardless of that flag's current
         value, same reasoning as public/register/index.html's own invite
         code field always being shown. #}
    <p class="text-sm text-muted">
      Currently in a closed beta — signing up needs an invite code.
    </p>
  </div>
  <script type="module">
    import { redirectIfLoggedIn } from "/-/session-redirect.js";
    redirectIfLoggedIn(document.getElementById("page-content"));
  </script>
  <script type="module" src="./demo-picker.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
